<title>BELGIUM: EU approves ELG Haniel buy of Jewometaal.</title>
<headline>EU approves ELG Haniel buy of Jewometaal.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Wednesday it had approved the proposed acquisition of the whole of Jewometaal Stainless Processing BV by ELG Haniel GmbH, a subsidiary of Franz Haniel &amp; Cie GmbH.</p>
<p>Both companies are active in trading and processing aluminium and copper scrap as well as stainless steel scrap, the Commission said in a statement.</p>
<p>It said that as far as aluminium and copper scrap were concerned, the overlap was limited to Britain. But the Commission considered that the companies' combined market share both in Britain and in Europe was &quot;unimportant&quot; and therefore the operation could be cleared.</p>
</text>
